# POST-HOC CAPTURE, 2026-08-24. This is NOT the original run's stdout.
#
# The relaxed round of 2026-08-22 was invoked by hand, one stage at a time: at
# that moment run_steering.sh did not derive its output paths from POLICY, so
# running the relaxed arm through the wrapper would have landed on the committed
# strict round. The wrapper is what tees each stage's stdout into provenance/, so
# this stage's stdout was never captured. The script has since been fixed and a
# relaxed run now writes this file itself.
#
# The lines below are the stdout of a re-run of that same stage, on 2026-08-24,
# from the same archived activation shards, the same script and the same seed
# (20260821). The build is deterministic and this was verified, not assumed: all
# six relaxed null vectors it wrote are byte-identical (md5) to the committed
# ones, and provenance/null_vectors_relaxed.json is byte-identical too. So the
# numbers are the numbers the original run printed; only the wall clock is not.
#
#   OMP_NUM_THREADS=8 CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES= <python> -u \
#       scripts/measurement/build_nulls.py --acts <shards> \
#       --out-dir results/crossgame-per-game-steering/vectors \
#       --policy relaxed --seed 20260821 \
#       --report results/crossgame-per-game-steering/provenance/null_vectors_relaxed.json
#
# provenance/null_vectors_strict.log is its own run's stdout and carries no header.
